@startuml template_method_forecasting
title Template Method (forecasting): todos los modelos siguen los mismos pasos
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam roundCorner 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FDF3EE
  BorderColor #444444
  ArrowColor #444444
}
hide empty members

abstract class DemandForecastModel <<AbstractClass>> {
  + name: str
  + label: str
  + min_points: int
  + forecast(series): float
  # _prepare(series): list[float]
  # _check_enough_data(series): None
  # {abstract} _estimate(series): float
  # _finalize(estimate): float
}

class MovingAverageModel <<ConcreteClass>> {
  # _estimate(series): float
}
class ExponentialSmoothingModel <<ConcreteClass>> {
  # _estimate(series): float
}
class LinearTrendModel <<ConcreteClass>> {
  + min_points = 2
  # _estimate(series): float
}

class ForecastPlanner <<Client>> {
  + compute(product_id, model_name): ForecastPlan
}

class InsufficientDemandData <<Exception>>

MovingAverageModel -up-|> DemandForecastModel
ExponentialSmoothingModel -up-|> DemandForecastModel
LinearTrendModel -up-|> DemandForecastModel
ForecastPlanner --> DemandForecastModel : forecast(series)
DemandForecastModel ..> InsufficientDemandData : lanza

note right of DemandForecastModel
  forecast() es el método plantilla:
  _prepare -> _check_enough_data
  -> _estimate -> _finalize
end note
@enduml
